{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications","id":1126656,"title":"Flight and it's complications","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-09T05:01:13-07:00","id":1126656,"title":"Flight and it's complications","content":"Ok something that has been bothering me for a while and I can't seem to find a satisfactory awnser for myself, so now it's time to ask the forums.<br /> <br /> Why is flight so hard and how do other arcana fit into it?<br /> <br /> First of all which spells can be used to fly? A mage can technically use Forces 2 &quot;Control Gravity&quot; to throw himself into the air, then cast it again to throw himself into another direction, etc. Not really the safest way of moving about but theoretically possible and appropriate for this level. At Forces 3 we have &quot;Telekinesis&quot; as a weaving practice, which makes sense and then at Forces 4 we have &quot;Levitation&quot; as a Pattering practice.... why though? What makes Levitation pattering? There is plenty of force around and all we really need to do with them is change their vectors around a bit, something which the weaving practice is specifically able to do (&quot;Turn Momentum&quot;). Why is Levitation a Forces 4 spell and not Forces 3, that seems to make no sense to me within the system.<br /> <br /> Now we go to other arcana and it gets even weirder. Matter 2 &quot;Shaping&quot; specifically mentions shaping materials in defiance of gravity, other Matter Spells such as Windstrike specifically move matter around telekintically (something that irks me in general, as I see movement covered under Forces rather than Matter, but I come from an Ascension background, so that probably influences my opinion there). So can't a matter mage build a hoverboard with Matter 2 using a variant on shaping, ruling the matter to move as he desires? Same with Life, if Matter can telekinetically move matter around, Life should be able to do the same with lifeforms. So are Matter and Life the better/easiers ways of flying? That doesn't seem right.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T05:38:40-07:00","id":1126668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications#post1126656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok something that has been bothering me for a while and I can't seem to find a satisfactory awnser for myself, so now it's time to ask the forums.<br /> <br /> Why is flight so hard and how do other arcana fit into it?<br /> <br /> First of all which spells can be used to fly? A mage can technically use Forces 2 &quot;Control Gravity&quot; to throw himself into the air, then cast it again to throw himself into another direction, etc. Not really the safest way of moving about but theoretically possible and appropriate for this level. At Forces 3 we have &quot;Telekinesis&quot; as a weaving practice, which makes sense and then at Forces 4 we have &quot;Levitation&quot; as a Pattering practice.... why though? What makes Levitation pattering? There is plenty of force around and all we really need to do with them is change their vectors around a bit, something which the weaving practice is specifically able to do (&quot;Turn Momentum&quot;). Why is Levitation a Forces 4 spell and not Forces 3, that seems to make no sense to me within the system.<br /> <br /> Now we go to other arcana and it gets even weirder. Matter 2 &quot;Shaping&quot; specifically mentions shaping materials in defiance of gravity, other Matter Spells such as Windstrike specifically move matter around telekintically (something that irks me in general, as I see movement covered under Forces rather than Matter, but I come from an Ascension background, so that probably influences my opinion there). So can't a matter mage build a hoverboard with Matter 2 using a variant on shaping, ruling the matter to move as he desires? Same with Life, if Matter can telekinetically move matter around, Life should be able to do the same with lifeforms. So are Matter and Life the better/easiers ways of flying? That doesn't seem right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Shaping's &quot;in defiance of gravity&quot; doesnt read to me like you can make the target fly/hover more that while shaping it you can make it &quot;defy&quot; gravity to make forms that otherwise wouldnt work. Ie making twisty columns that spiral over themselves out of steel that normally would collapse on itself.<br /> <br /> Forces is the goto arcana for flying because its in its Purview as movement. Life can give flight via shapechanging into something with wings capable of flight. Matter's windstrike can use air/waters natural ability to move to force it to cause damage just like it can control objects via remote control. I wouldnt allow windstrike to be used on say a stone that isnt capable of movement on its own for example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T06:05:55-07:00","id":1126669,"title":"","content":"You can get airborne if you're in Twilight by just walking up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T07:14:49-07:00","id":1126690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1126669#post1126669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can get airborne if you're in Twilight by just walking up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Walking kinda implies stepping on something, and the rules on Twilight specifically says that only beings with appropriate forms are capable of flight in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T07:21:11-07:00","id":1126693,"title":"","content":"Well, there's this bad, bad idea but potentially super fun way of &quot;flying&quot; using Space to alter your vectors of up, down and forward to alter how gravity affects you. So you will technically be &quot;falling&quot; upwards or forward, but who will tell, eh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T07:34:52-07:00","id":1126701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1126668#post1126668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Shaping's &quot;in defiance of gravity&quot; doesnt read to me like you can make the target fly/hover more that while shaping it you can make it &quot;defy&quot; gravity to make forms that otherwise wouldnt work. Ie making twisty columns that spiral over themselves out of steel that normally would collapse on itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, it doesn't say anything about telekinesis like effect there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Matter's windstrike can use air/waters natural ability to move to force it to cause damage just like it can control objects via remote control. </div> </div> </div>But there is no natural ability to move for air or water. Or at least no natural ability that any other form of matter doesn't possess. The difference between different aggregate states of matter is more one of cohesion, not of being able to move in a bulk. So what Windstrike does is specifically moving air/water in a fashion the mage desires... which is essentially telekinesis. The mage doesn't change the matter at all, the only thing he changes is the kinetic energy of the matter. Which to me sounds like it should be a forces effect, but Matter has lots of effects that makes matter actually move in any desire the mage wishes.... so why not flight by telling a skateboard underneath you to move up?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldnt allow windstrike to be used on say a stone that isnt capable of movement on its own for example. </div> </div> </div>That's just piercing Earth. Which only really seems to be a pattering spell because it inflicts lethal damage. Even then in the end it raises the same question. If you can make the Earth move and strike out against others, why not flight? It's just weird that Matter would be able to move anything around as it wishes, but flight is somehow prohibited unless it's a gas you're affecting.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T07:41:41-07:00","id":1126704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1126690#post1126690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Walking kinda implies stepping on something, and the rules on Twilight specifically says that only beings with appropriate forms are capable of flight in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, I only remembered that there isn't any gravity in Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T08:37:33-07:00","id":1126727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1126701#post1126701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair point, it doesn't say anything about telekinesis like effect there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But there is no natural ability to move for air or water. Or at least no natural ability that any other form of matter doesn't possess. The difference between different aggregate states of matter is more one of cohesion, not of being able to move in a bulk. So what Windstrike does is specifically moving air/water in a fashion the mage desires... which is essentially telekinesis. The mage doesn't change the matter at all, the only thing he changes is the kinetic energy of the matter. Which to me sounds like it should be a forces effect, but Matter has lots of effects that makes matter actually move in any desire the mage wishes.... so why not flight by telling a skateboard underneath you to move up?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's just piercing Earth. Which only really seems to be a pattering spell because it inflicts lethal damage. Even then in the end it raises the same question. If you can make the Earth move and strike out against others, why not flight? It's just weird that Matter would be able to move anything around as it wishes, but flight is somehow prohibited unless it's a gas you're affecting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>On a purely physical explanation level: Matter deals with manipulating energy on a subatomic level, while Forces deals with energy on a macroscopic level. On a metaphysical level: matter can influence the way &quot;stuff&quot; behaves, while forces can be used to move &quot;stuff&quot;. In any way for some examples both arcana are quite close to each other.<br /> Windstrike can be achieved by conglomerating air particals very fast into a certain position. Which creates a force. Force times matter equals a momentum. The momentum is what actually hurts you. You can also use forces to accelerate air particles very fast to create the same momentum. That is basically what one of the two possibilities of kinetic strike does. So yeah. You can have the same effect with two different arcana. But both manipulate something under their arcanas purview, so it's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T08:42:43-07:00","id":1126729,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> ,<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know if it's an Ascension thing (I don't know that system well) but I do think you are getting hung up on some misunderstandings. Awakening magic works on symbolism, not physics. Wind has the innate property of moving because that's what makes it wind rather than air. I like to think of it as Objects in a programming sense:<br /> <br /> Object Wind has the following properties:<br /> * is made of air<br /> * is transparent<br /> * moves over the surface of the earth<br /> * *other things like that*<br /> <br /> So a Ruling spell lets you make wind move because you are Ruling it to use its 'can move' quality. On the other hand the symbol of a rock doesn't inherently contain the 'can move' property so it takes at least weaving to give it that property.<br /> <br /> As for Levitation, as far as I can tell, it is just a badly written spell. Without the Reach effects it does exactly the same thing as Telekinesis but seems to be written to target people rather than objects (a distinction that mattered in 1e but shouldn't in 2e).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T09:46:20-07:00","id":1126743,"title":"","content":"In general I didn't want to complain that flight can be done by Arcana outside of Forces. That's fine, I'm mostly confused about how Matter seems to be able to more easily do it at a cursory view and why it's so complicated to do with Forces (looking specifically at Levitation which in my mind should be a weaving practice).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1126729#post1126729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5241\" data-vbnamecard=\"5241\">Flinty</a> ,<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know if it's an Ascension thing (I don't know that system well) but I do think you are getting hung up on some misunderstandings. Awakening magic works on symbolism, not physics. Wind has the innate property of moving because that's what makes it wind rather than air. I like to think of it as Objects in a programming sense:</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a rather nice explanation actually, thank you. The problem I have with this though is that then having a Forces as one of the Arcana becomes weird. If you go with the elements have such and such properties, you could easily say fire is just another element and lightning is just an expression of fire and air fusing etc. In that case it'd make more sense to have an &quot;Element&quot; Arcanum. But maybe I'm overcomplicating things.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T10:41:56-07:00","id":1126767,"title":"","content":"Another distinction between Telekinesis and Levitation is that it no longer requires concentration and an Instant action to make things move. I feel like that could probably have just been a Reach on Telekinesis and cut Levitation though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T11:07:12-07:00","id":1126776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1126743#post1126743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That is a rather nice explanation actually, thank you. The problem I have with this though is that then having a Forces as one of the Arcana becomes weird. If you go with the elements have such and such properties, you could easily say fire is just another element and lightning is just an expression of fire and air fusing etc. In that case it'd make more sense to have an &quot;Element&quot; Arcanum. But maybe I'm overcomplicating things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Where did the word element come into it? Everything has that symbol based pattern system not just elements. The same Object principal applies to everything in reality and each Arcana covers certain aspects of each of those Objects.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> Two affected primarily by Life:<br /> <br /> Object Dog:<br /> * is an animal<br /> * eats meat<br /> * has blood<br /> * has fur<br /> * has four legs<br /> * is man's best friend<br /> * etc.<br /> <br /> Object Mage:<br /> * is human (Object Human has a whole set of its own properties that Mages inherit)<br /> * has Gnosis<br /> * signed his name to a Watchtower<br /> * has a nimbus<br /> * etc.<br /> <br /> One affected primarily by Death:<br /> <br /> Object Ghost:<br /> * Was created from a human<br /> * is made of death-attuned Ephemera<br /> * has a Rank<br /> * posses Manifestations<br /> * consumes Essence<br /> * etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T19:45:44-07:00","id":1126937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1126727#post1126727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a purely physical explanation level: Matter deals with manipulating energy on a subatomic level, while Forces deals with energy on a macroscopic level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter is super-atomic, once you get to the subatomic (and, arguably, atomic) level you're back to Forces again.<br /> <br /> <br /> @OP: the reason Flight is Patterning is because you're imbuing something with the property of being able to manipulate gravity in a way that gives flight, whereas with Weaving you're actively changing how gravity affects the object in a pseudo-dynamic way.<br /> <br /> If you'd like a fiction example it's the difference between a Witch riding a broom (Weaving) and being able to fly without the broom (Patterning).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T01:19:20-07:00","id":1127006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1126937#post1126937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Matter is super-atomic, once you get to the subatomic (and, arguably, atomic) level you're back to Forces again.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Pretty much everything you can do with matter can physically be explained via manipulation of the (binding)-forces between atoms. I don't see a single spell in the forces section, which does anything like that. Concerning atoms, Matter is the scalpel and Forces the sledgehammer figuratively.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T01:49:12-07:00","id":1127009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1126937#post1126937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@OP: the reason Flight is Patterning is because you're imbuing something with the property of being able to manipulate gravity in a way that gives flight, whereas with Weaving you're actively changing how gravity affects the object in a pseudo-dynamic way.<br /> <br /> If you'd like a fiction example it's the difference between a Witch riding a broom (Weaving) and being able to fly without the broom (Patterning).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an artificial speed bump between object and person, 2e was supposed to do away with those. It really doesn't seem the two spells do anything different except Levitation grants greater control and ease of use which ought to be a function of Reach, not Practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T02:16:37-07:00","id":1127017,"title":"","content":"Telekinesis provides a force that can be used to manipulate an object any way that you could by yourself, but it's limited in how much it can lift because you have to assign potency to strength.<br /> <br /> Levitation can only move things, but you can potentially levitate an entire truck without much difficulty (advanced scale means you just need -4 to the roll, instead of - 26 or so).<br /> <br /> They're fundamentally different effects and human/object distinction has absolutely nothing to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T02:26:35-07:00","id":1127020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1127006#post1127006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. Pretty much everything you can do with matter can physically be explained via manipulation of the (binding)-forces between atoms. I don't see a single spell in the forces section, which does anything like that. Concerning atoms, Matter is the scalpel and Forces the sledgehammer figuratively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, Matter ignores all of the actual energy and forces of such a change. Matter is the &quot;cheat&quot;, so to speak, allowing you to simply <i>do</i> on a large scale, such as converting lead into gold. Forces could also turn lead into gold but would have to do so by mucking about with the actual strong force to do the same. Matter is the chemical and the alchemical, Forces is forces and energy. Matter isn't explicable by manipulation of fundamental forces because it explicitly bypass such forces and simply acts on things that fall under the symbolic header of Matter; conversely Forces works on anything under the symbolic header of Forces... which includes forces.<br /> <br /> And Forces most certainly does interact at the subatomic level: all the Electricity spells, all the Heat spells and all the spells that affect Radiation (solidly in Force's wheelhouse, including alpha particles which are basically Helium nuclei). On the other hand, I don't think anyone considers quarks or electrons to be &quot;matter&quot;, nor would a single proton in a nucleus be manipulable by Matter (unless it was an H<sup>+</sup> ion, I guess).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1127009#post1127009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an artificial speed bump between object and person, 2e was supposed to do away with those. It really doesn't seem the two spells do anything different except Levitation grants greater control and ease of use which ought to be a function of Reach, not Practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you also consider Shapechanging a speedbumped version of Transform Life? Because to me they have the same relationship as Levitation to Telekinesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T02:35:42-07:00","id":1127021,"title":"","content":"Plus telekinesis conjures a blob of force that you can do whatever you like with. Levitation grants a <i>specific</i> object the ability to float. That's textbook patterning.<br /> <br /> Hell, if anything Telekinesis is technically a Making spell. It &quot;makes&quot; a force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:00:05-07:00","id":1127037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1127021#post1127021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus telekinesis conjures a blob of force that you can do whatever you like with. Levitation grants a <i>specific</i> object the ability to float. That's textbook patterning.<br /> <br /> Hell, if anything Telekinesis is technically a Making spell. It &quot;makes&quot; a force.</div> </div> </div> </div>Telekinesis has been stated before to just change the vectors of the myriad of forces all around, no need for a making practice. That said how is Levitation textbook pattering? That's the main question here, when does the Levitation spell ever pattern a Force? It doesn't change one force into another or anything like that. At best it gives a force slightly different properties, which is straightforward weaving.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:13:29-07:00","id":1127040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1127037#post1127037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Telekinesis has been stated before to just change the vectors of the myriad of forces all around, no need for a making practice. That said how is Levitation textbook pattering? That's the main question here, when does the Levitation spell ever pattern a Force? It doesn't change one force into another or anything like that. At best it gives a force slightly different properties, which is straightforward weaving.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's changing traditional terrestrial locomotion into 3-D locomotion (changing &quot;how something moves&quot; into a completely different way of moving). Yes, this can be achieved at lower dot levels through exploitation of current knowledge of physics, but this is the &quot;brute force&quot; method of altering the concept at a high levels which means the Supernal is doing more of the heavy-lifting in achieving the result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:18:12-07:00","id":1127041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1127040#post1127040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's changing traditional terrestrial locomotion into 3-D locomotion (changing &quot;how something moves&quot; into a completely different way of moving). Yes, this can be achieved at lower dot levels through exploitation of current knowledge of physics, but this is the &quot;brute force&quot; method of altering the concept at a high levels which means the Supernal is doing more of the heavy-lifting in achieving the result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting approach. That could explain it, though I have to question... is that really pattering? Pattering is usually turning one thing into something (radically) different. This just expands normal modes of movement to incorporate the third dimension so to speak. Adding a new property to an existing form of movement... which should be weaving (in 2E anyway).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:24:45-07:00","id":1127042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1127041#post1127041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting approach. That could explain it, though I have to question... is that really pattering? Pattering is usually turning one thing into something (radically) different. This just expands normal modes of movement to incorporate the third dimension so to speak. Adding a new property to an existing form of movement... which should be weaving (in 2E anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that being able to soar through the air with no need for specially tailored physical attributes (e.g. wings and hollow bones) in defiance of the naturally existing laws of physics would be radically different from traditional locomotion via moving our legs and using our feet to push off the ground, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:37:49-07:00","id":1127045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1127042#post1127042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that being able to soar through the air with no need for specially tailored physical attributes (e.g. wings and hollow bones) in defiance of the naturally existing laws of physics would be radically different from traditional locomotion via moving our legs and using our feet to push off the ground, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well defying naturally existing laws of physics is well within weavings purview. You can outright switch around vectors of force. You can turn solids into gases. You can make air conduct electricity. Wether flight or not its still just movement. If you wanted to turn movement into heat, that'd be a pattering practice (ala Friction Curse).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:49:38-07:00","id":1127046,"title":"","content":"Movement into heat should be possible with Ruling. That's something that always happens so you just need to turn up the rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:52:07-07:00","id":1127047,"title":"","content":"Ruling would increase the conversion rate through friction to the maximum physically possible, perfecting could push it beyond that and patterin outright changes movement into heat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T04:59:30-07:00","id":1127051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1127045#post1127045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well defying naturally existing laws of physics is well within weavings purview. You can outright switch around vectors of force. You can turn solids into gases. You can make air conduct electricity. Wether flight or not its still just movement. If you wanted to turn movement into heat, that'd be a pattering practice (ala Friction Curse).</div> </div> </div> </div>But linear kinetic energy and heat energy are both just types of energy, wouldn't that be Weaving, too? What's the point of Matter since everything is energy (Forces)? And, really, what even is the difference between &quot;time&quot; and &quot;space&quot;, time has every property space does, you can even use the same units for both if you multiply time by the speed of light! At some point you just have to draw a line and say &quot;yes, this thing is a different thing at the Supernal level&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, some of this is simply the regime in which the imago is operating, Levitation's imago is formed in a regime of thought that ignores the modern physical understanding of the world for a more heuristic/wysiwyg approach. Again, you could emulate the same effect at a lower level practice if you wanted to jump through the hoops, the point is that using Patterning is an easier, brute force way of doing things that simply overwrites the rules rather than exploiting loopholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:28:14-07:00","id":1127138,"title":"","content":"And all of that is why thinking in terms of Physics is wrong. Mage doesn't work that way, it is all about symbolism. Atoms, linear connect energy, and all that don't matter.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> is correct, I read the spells again and see what he means about Telekinesis. It weaves the ambient kinetic force into a controllable ball that can then be used to manipulate other things. It doesn't have a withstand rating for this reason, you never target a person with the spell, but you could utilize the force you are controlling to target a person. You are Weaving the property 'controllable' into the force and then you can control it.<br /> <br /> Levitation is Patterning because you are patterning the forces that exist in the target from being static, hold them in place forces to move around freely forces.<br /> <br /> Both the witch's broom and witch flying alone examples would be levitation, the broom would just be an Imbued item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Clarified the Patterning explanation a bit. 08-10-2017, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T22:03:39-08:00","id":1167516,"title":"","content":"Hello, I know this is four months dead and all but I have a question. Is it then possible using shaping on say, for example, my characters clothing or outfit to essentially grip it with the spell, up the duration and so on then allow flight based on moving the outfit? We are still learning this new edition, but my reasoning here is its like how magneto flies, using his power to lift his metal infused costume. <br /> <br /> One scene had my guy flying off a roof top with shaping, then using remote control to take over a helicopter to wipe out the enemies he just escaped from.. <br /> <br /> If flight with shaping is possible, does it just use the character's speed rating? What if I wanted to use shaping on say, a dirtbike's chassis to fly while riding that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T22:18:23-08:00","id":1167520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1167516#post1167516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I know this is four months dead and all but I have a question. Is it then possible using shaping on say, for example, my characters clothing or outfit to essentially grip it with the spell, up the duration and so on then allow flight based on moving the outfit? We are still learning this new edition, but my reasoning here is its like how magneto flies, using his power to lift his metal infused costume.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reasonably certain the &quot;in defiance of gravity&quot; bit is narrative justification for being able to e.g. stretch a tendril of clay out far past the point where it ought to collapse under its own weight, not Actual Real-Ass Levitation, being that this is a pure-Matter spell for shaping physical matter rather than a more forceful version of Lodestone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T00:02:14-08:00","id":1167537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1167516#post1167516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I know this is four months dead and all but I have a question. Is it then possible using shaping on say, for example, my characters clothing or outfit to essentially grip it with the spell, up the duration and so on then allow flight based on moving the outfit? We are still learning this new edition, but my reasoning here is its like how magneto flies, using his power to lift his metal infused costume.<br /> <br /> One scene had my guy flying off a roof top with shaping, then using remote control to take over a helicopter to wipe out the enemies he just escaped from..<br /> <br /> If flight with shaping is possible, does it just use the character's speed rating? What if I wanted to use shaping on say, a dirtbike's chassis to fly while riding that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think grafting together something with Forces + Life and/or Mind might be a good way to put together a Duration based flight spell, whereby a person controls their vectors either by bodily instinct (like a superhero) or thought (like Magneto).<br /> <br /> You might also use Potency to increase maximum speed, either by a flat table or by some modification of your base speed and use free fall damage rules for any collisions that might occur - unless you throw in another forces spell, like a shield, to help you mitigate any unforeseen crashes.<br /> <br /> Not sure if this is at all useful for your character, but I think something like flight should be rudimentary for a mage. It just might be primitive when compared to all other modes of transportation.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'd also like to add that one form of interpreting gravity is as acceleration. Or so I'm led to believe, if my Brian Greene books (the Elegant Universe and the Fabric of the Cosmos) are correct. I believe the example in the book has to do with sudden gravity applied to an object (or person) floating in the vacuum of space. The applied gravity would have a similar, if not identical, effect to suddenly accelerating in the direction of the thing you're falling toward.<br /> <br /> Ergo, could negate and apply gravity directionally with Forces. Heck, if you combined Forces + Space + Life and/or Mind, you could use Space to precisely control the vector at which the force of gravity applies with the use of your body and/or mind.<br /> <br /> At least, this is something I'd be cool with allowing. It seems intuitive enough.<br /> <br /> If you want to be really cool about it, you could look up the velocity at which the guy in the rocket sledge suffered horrendous bruising. This could be sort of an upper limit on flight speed without mitigating for things like friction or putting a spell on yourself to withstand the pressure wave of trying to cut through the atmosphere at sea level density. Not to mention freezing your face off or asphyxiating from high altitude flight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":11166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","user":"kryptonitekrusher","date":". 12-14-2017, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T00:07:20-08:00","id":1167539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1167537#post1167537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think grafting together something with Forces + Life and/or Mind might be a good way to put together a Duration based flight spell, whereby a person controls their vectors either by bodily instinct (like a superhero) or thought (like Magneto).<br /> <br /> You might also use Potency to increase maximum speed, either by a flat table or by some modification of your base speed and use free fall damage rules for any collisions that might occur - unless you throw in another forces spell, like a shield, to help you mitigate any unforeseen crashes.<br /> <br /> Not sure if this is at all useful for your character, but I think something like flight should be rudimentary for a mage. It just might be primitive when compared to all other modes of transportation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah this is kinda where I was going, I have forces 2 and aim to make it part of a custom legacy for my moros later. I figure, if I can lift a boulder, shape it into something, move it and more.. why can't I be on it at the same time, or in it. I figured it was just slow, my guy's speed is 9 so I was just using it that way. It's not superman or a higher practice of flight.. but with air control and other stuff, I honestly didn't see an issue. I just wish it was stated clearer. You could even argue using shaping and state change to move air around/under you, making it solid enough to lift you. Shaping just did it in my mind like levitation would, not the actual levitation spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1614-berdryn","name":"Berdryn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T01:01:23-08:00","id":1167547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Berdryn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1126656-flight-and-it-s-complications?p=1167539#post1167539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah this is kinda where I was going, I have forces 2 and aim to make it part of a custom legacy for my moros later. I figure, if I can lift a boulder, shape it into something, move it and more.. why can't I be on it at the same time, or in it. I figured it was just slow, my guy's speed is 9 so I was just using it that way. It's not superman or a higher practice of flight.. but with air control and other stuff, I honestly didn't see an issue. I just wish it was stated clearer. You could even argue using shaping and state change to move air around/under you, making it solid enough to lift you. Shaping just did it in my mind like levitation would, not the actual levitation spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be willing to accept columns of &quot;solid air&quot; reinforced by magic. The only other issue you might run into is figuring out how much weight this partition of air can hold.<br /> <br /> You'd be using your magic to make this new and unique structure, so anything that applies weight or force to it would need to contend with your magic. Forces can get away with it because it can negate gravity as a factor.<br /> <br /> For shaping Matter to support weight it otherwise couldn't, like air, I'd be tempted to use Potency as a rough equivalent to Strength lifting/push/push on wheels.<br /> <br /> Your column of air might also need some rough estimation of it's maximum distance. Some reasonable multiple of it's scale factor.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you could literally have this column of air follow you around like a giant invisible snake carrying you and your boulder on its head - at this point, however, I think you might be better off with getting an ephemeral being to possess your boulder and fly you around.<br /> <br /> I can think of 3 different convoluted ways of making this work with Matter, but I think getting an invisible entity is the quickest short-cut. Otherwise you'll need to build something your ST is cool with based on a bunch of stuff like the range of your air snake or whether or not it moves autonomously or by your will and command.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}